    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326-a1-a14">

                <pb facs="0510" n="470" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg470"/>

                <head>[Enclosure No. 14.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>83 <hi rendition="#small-caps">Collins Street West,
                                Melbourne,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 3, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> On Monday, the 2d instant, I attended at
                    your chambers with Mr. Blanchard, the American consul, and left certain
                    depositions (which he had caused to be taken) with your secretary, Mr. Chomley,
                    for your perusal, with the view to establish that the Shenandoah is in fact the
                    Sea King, <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c.</hi></p>
                <p>Mr. Blanchard considered it to be his duty to place the depositions above
                    referred to in your hands, so as to enable the government to take such steps in
                    the matter as they may think necessary.<hi rendition="#italic">&gt;</hi></p>
                <p>Mr. Blanchard has instructed me to state that he will, on hearing from you, be
                    happy to attend you with the further evidence he has obtained in this
                    matter.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOSEPH G. DUFFETT.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Attorney General,</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
